  "reachedBy": {
    "why": "The step is React state in components-legacy/booking/BookingWizard.tsx via lib/booking-context. That component reads no searchParams, so ?step=staff cannot select this screen and returns step one instead. The wizard has to be driven.",
    "salon": "cuts-and-culture (id 5784b1ab-7314-437a-a608-01a729f02cdd). Verified it has MORE THAN ONE staff member before using it: 3 active rows in staff_members (Jonas, Marco, Tim), so BookingWizard's `hasStaffStep = staffList.length > 1` is true and the step is not skipped.",
    "service": "Herrenschnitt, CHF 45, 30 min. Chosen because staff_services maps all three stylists to it (Herrenschnitt, Bart trimmen and Coupe & Bart are the only three mapped services, each to all three stylists), so StaffStep's `capable` filter drops nobody and the list renders at full width. It also carries zero rows in service_options and zero in service_addons, so the add button commits straight to the cart instead of opening ServiceDetailSheet.",
    "steps": [
      "1. Claude_Browser preview_start + navigate to http://localhost:3457/de/salon/cuts-and-culture/booking in tab-114, then tabs_select to FRONT the tab (this pane throttles rAF in background tabs).",
      "2. resize_window 402x844 on that tab.",
      "3. On the services step, click the add (Hinzufuegen) button inside the row whose text contains 'Herrenschnitt'. Bottom bar then reads 'CHF 45 / 1 Artikel / 30 Min' and the Weiter button becomes enabled.",
      "4. Click Weiter. h1 changes from 'Services auswaehlen' to 'Stylist:in auswaehlen'.",
      "5. Settle: sample the settle signature from scripts/measure-sections.mjs twice, 3 s apart. Both returned '19|2000|9408', two consecutive identical samples, so settled is true.",
      "6. Run the extractSections function body from scripts/measure-sections.mjs via javascript_tool and save the result under the same top-level keys."
    ],
    "inputMethod": "The clicks in steps 3 and 4 were dispatched as HTMLElement.click() through mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, NOT through mcp__Claude_Browser__computer. The computer left_click action timed out after 30 s on three consecutive attempts (once by ref, twice by coordinate) and delivered nothing: the category pill's aria-pressed and background were unchanged afterwards. The page itself was responsive throughout (javascript_tool round-tripped in well under a second, document.getAnimations() reported 0 running animations, and document.elementFromPoint returned the real button at each target coordinate), so the failure is in the pane's input path, not the page. Recorded because it changes what the measurement proves: the React onClick handlers ran, but no real pointer event, hover state or focus-visible state was exercised.",
    "notMeasured": "The 'Profil ansehen' link opens StaffProfileSheet, a separate overlay. It was not opened, so nothing here describes it.",
